From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 21:00:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] VideoPlayer: a chapter seek seeks the subtitle file too

A seek in time also seeks the demuxer of a subtitle file, but a seek to
a chapter did not. After a jump back, the subtitles of the file stayed
missing until playback got back to where the file had been read to;
after a jump forward, the subtitles of the chapters jumped over were
decoded first, and old ones flashed on the screen.

The subtitle file is now sought to where the chapter seek landed (the
start that the demuxer or the input stream gives), backward as a seek
in time back is, in every way a chapter seek ends (FinishChapterSeek()).

From matthane's change for CoreELEC (CoreELEC/xbmc commit 1f443a651f,
"VideoPlayer: seek external subtitles on chapter seeks").
---
 xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoPlayer.cpp | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoPlayer.cpp b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoPlayer.cpp
index ce72199..d521aca 100644
--- a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoPlayer.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoPlayer.cpp
@@ -4351,6 +4351,12 @@ void CVideoPlayer::HandleMessages()
         FlushBuffers(start, true, true);
         if (start != DVD_NOPTS_VALUE)
         {
+          // a subtitle file is sought with the video, as a seek in time does: else it stays where
+          // it was read to, without its subtitles after a jump back, and with the old ones of
+          // the chapters jumped over decoded (and flashed) after a jump forward
+          if (m_pSubtitleDemuxer &&
+              !m_pSubtitleDemuxer->SeekTime(DVD_TIME_TO_MSEC(start), true))
+            CLog::Log(LOGDEBUG, "failed to seek the subtitle demuxer to chapter {}", newChapter);
           const int64_t targetTime{
               m_Edl.GetTimeWithoutCuts(std::chrono::milliseconds(DVD_TIME_TO_MSEC(start))).count()};
           offset = targetTime - beforeSeek;
